{
  "position": "evidence_shown_is_insufficient",
  "answer": "No instance can be identified from what was supplied. This invocation received no prior record, no deliberation history, no adoption log, and no statement of the operator's preferences on any past outcome—only the explicit note that nothing beyond the question was selected. Without that material I cannot name an adoption that ran against the operator's stated preference, nor can I responsibly assert that none exists. I am also not the operator (Stephen Reed) and hold none of the credentials at issue, so I cannot commit him to escrow, veto divestment, or any other structural change, nor can I file or number a defect on his behalf. The question's premise that a party to this round can either surface the binding example or bind the operator is therefore unanswerable on the given evidence; the honest output is that the evidence shown is insufficient.",
  "where_i_expect_another_party_to_disagree": "A party with access to the full hash-anchored record might claim that such a counter-preferential adoption already exists and that my insufficiency finding is therefore too narrow; alternatively the operator or another surface might argue that the demand for credential divestment is the wrong test of whether the process is governance versus advice.",
  "what_would_change_my_answer": "Provision of the actual deliberation/adoption record (or relevant excerpts) sufficient to verify whether any outcome was adopted against a contemporaneous stated operator preference; or a clear, in-record commitment document from the operator himself that I am authorized to treat as binding. Either would let me move from insufficiency to a substantive yes/no on the two halves of the question."
}

